    "method": "Four installation blocks (before, after, after, before). For each, reinstall, start and discard one warm-up process, then launch two fresh processes. Before each launch force-stop the benchmark and wait four seconds; keep it in foreground after it prints its result until the next force-stop. Each process starts with an empty lunar cache. OS file caches may be warm. This tests the calendar with the home day painter, not the entire example app.",
    "workload": "Cold July 2026 in onlyCurrentMonth; 12 July jumps (2027–2038) before awaiting endOfFrame; 24 July jumps (2039–2062) each followed by endOfFrame; then 42 disabled-date queries (21 hits spread across 10,000 entries and 21 misses), ten grids per batch, one warm-up batch and five timed batches. Lookup excludes construction.",
    "aggregation": "Times are in microseconds except androidLaunchTotalMs (Android am start -W TotalTime in milliseconds). dartEntryToFirstRasterFinishUs uses the Dart entry wall timestamp and the first Flutter frame rasterFinishWallTime. firstRasterFinishToTimingCallbackUs measures the subsequent callback delivery. Median over four per-version process measurements, summing the 24 displayed-year intervals per process first. For disabled42LookupsUs pool the 20 batch times per version, divide by 10 grids, then take the median. coldFirstRasterNotificationUs is elapsed time from Dart main to Flutter first rasterized notification. firstBuildUs comes from FrameTiming. endOfFrame intervals include scheduler wait and post-frame work, and are not presentation times. Cache values count LunarMetadata entries.",
